# Brewfile.linux — CLI layer for Bazzite / Linux
#
# Source: gyatfiles/scripts/packages/Brewfile (macOS) + install-arch.sh PACMAN_PACKAGES.
# Homebrew ships preinstalled on Bazzite and is Universal Blue's documented installer
# for CLI/TUI apps, so this file is the whole CLI layer -- no rpm-ostree layering.
#
# Apply:  brew bundle --file=~/gyatfiles/scripts/packages/Brewfile.linux
# Check:  brew bundle check --file=... ; Prune: brew bundle cleanup --file=...
#
# NOT here, deliberately:
#   - casks           -> macOS-only. GUI apps on Bazzite are flatpaks.
#   - coreutils, openssl@3, pkgconf, autoconf, glib, icu4c, harfbuzz, libxml2,
#     libmtp, libraqm, opus, pillow, protobuf, miniupnpc, squashfs
#                     -> these exist to patch up macOS. On Linux they are the system
#                        or arrive as transitive deps. Installing them shadows the
#                        distro copy and is how you get subtle ABI breakage.
#   - carthage, cliclick, displayplacer, imagesnap, swiftlint, xcbeautify,
#     xcode-build-server, xcodegen, firefoxpwa, uniclipboard, qt
#                     -> macOS/Xcode-only or better from the distro.
#   - mysql@8.4, postgresql@14, memcached
#                     -> servers belong in podman/distrobox, not on the host PATH.
#   - zsh             -> must be a real login shell for chsh, so it is layered in the
#                        bootc image, NOT installed here. See the migration wargame.
#   - ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd -> font casks are macOS-only; the Nerd Font is installed by
#                        scripts/linux/packages.sh from the distro instead.
#   - ghostty         -> NO Linux formula (checked: cask only, macOS-only). Stays a gap;
#                        install from the distro or build it. ~/bin/ghostty-gamescope is
#                        only a wrapper and does not provide the terminal itself.
#   - claude-code     -> cask only, macOS-only. Installed by scripts/linux/ai-tools.sh.
#   - codex           -> no formula. Installed by scripts/linux/ai-tools.sh.
#   - opencode        -> HAS a Linux formula, but is installed by ai-tools.sh alongside
#                        the rest of the AI stack so there is one source of truth.

